                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p To make this precise:
          %ul
            %li
              A definable group is just a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"} group object
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Def
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Def}(T)
            %li
              A definable groupoid is just a groupoid object, i.e. an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+groupoid"} internal groupoid
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Def
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Def}(T)
            %li
              A definable ring is just a semigroup object in the category of abelian group objects of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Def
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Def}(T)
            %li
              A definable category is just a category object, i.e. an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+category"} internal category
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Def
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Def}(T)
          %p
            Since groups, groupoids, rings, and categories can be given by algebraic theories, a definition (modulo having
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elimination+of+imaginaries"} EI
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is just an interpretation of one of those theories in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is just a logical functor from the walking models of one of these to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Def
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Def}(T)
          %h3#remarks Remarks
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Evaluating the unit of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Makkai+duality"} Makkai duality
                adjunction at
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                yields
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Def
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Hom
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi Ult
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Mod
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Def}(T) \simeq \operatorname{Hom}_{\mathbf{Ult}}(\mathbf{Mod}(T), \mathbf{Set})
                the category of
                %span.newWikiWord
                  ultrafunctors
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/ultrafunctors"} ?
                from the category of models (logical functors
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi Def
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi T
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi Set
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Def}(T) \to \mathbf{Set}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Set}
                viewed as
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ultracategories"} ultracategories
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∈
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Def
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathbf{Def}(T)
                with a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+of+points"} functor of points
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mo ↦
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi M
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M \mapsto X(M)
                on the category of models.
            %li
              %p
                The fact that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/external+axiom+of+choice"} external axiom of choice
                (all epimorphisms split) holds in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Set}
                if and only if every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful"} fully faithful
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+surjective"} essentially surjective
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
                between
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small"} small
                categories is a true
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
                can be word-for-word internalized to
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi Def
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi T
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Def}(T)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                has definable Skolem functions if and only if every fully faithful essentially surjective definable functor between definable categories admits a
                = succeed "." do
                  %span.newWikiWord
                    pseudoinverse
                    %a{:href => "/nlab/new/pseudoinverse"} ?
            %li
              %p
                With a suitable amount of choice (definable Skolem functions, for example) Freyd’s general adjoint functor theorem also carries over word-for-word to the setting of internal categories in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi Def
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi T
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Def}(T)
            %li
              %p
                In particular, there is much studied case of
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong definable groups
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "#PeterzilPillay"} Peterzil-Pillay
          %h2#properties Properties
          .num_defn
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              There is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijective
              correspondence between internal imaginary sorts of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              and definable concrete groupoids with a single isomorphism class, up to bi-interpretability over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              for the internal imaginary sorts and Hrushovski-equivalence for the definable concrete groupoids.
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#Hrushovski"}> Hrushovski 2006, Th.3.2
            ).
